# Line endings belong to the repository, not to whoever checked it out.
#
# Without this file the working tree depends on each machine's core.autocrlf,
# which is how .editorconfig's `end_of_line` rule came to be true on Windows
# and false on the Linux CI runner: the same command passed locally and failed
# in CI on the same commit. The repository stores LF, so LF is what every
# checkout gets (ADR-028).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Written by other tools, byte for byte.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.tgz binary

# The tracker shapes fixture holds CRLF breaks and a byte order mark on purpose: the tracker's SQL copy is held to
# the file byte for byte (PROMPT-JOBHUNT-TRACKER-SQL), so git must not touch its line ends.
functions/jobhunt.Tests/Fixtures/tracker-shapes.csv binary
